# breadcrumbs.zd — where you are, and how you got here.
#
# Three decisions, all of them about markup that a `Row` of `Link`s does
# not have:
#
#   1. A `Navigation`, so the trail is a landmark a reader can jump to.
#   2. A `NumberedList`, because the trail is ordered and the order is the
#      information. A screen reader announces "list, 3 items" and the
#      position of each, which is the hierarchy read out loud.
#   3. The last step is `Text` and not a `Link`. A link to the page you are
#      already on is a control that does nothing, and it is the one step in
#      the trail that is not somewhere else.
#
# `title is "Breadcrumb"` names the landmark. `aria-label` is what a
# hand-written breadcrumb uses and it is not spellable here (README), but
# the accessible-name computation falls back to `title` when there is no
# label, so the landmark is named — by a lower-priority route, and named.
#
# WHAT IS MISSING: `aria-current="page"` on the last step, which is how a
# breadcrumb says "this one is the current page" rather than leaving it to
# be inferred from its being the only one that is not a link. Hyphenated,
# so unspellable.

# One step of the trail. Declared here rather than by the caller so that
# the shape `Breadcrumbs` walks is the shape the module documents; a caller
# imports it alongside the component.
record Crumb
    label is Text
    href  is Text

component Breadcrumbs with trail, here, class, linkClass, currentClass
    Navigation class is class, title is "Breadcrumb"
        NumberedList
            each step in trail
                Item
                    Link step.href, class is linkClass
                        Text step.label
            Item
                Text here, class is currentClass
